# linux-rpi4

Cross-compiled Raspberry Pi 4 (BCM2711) kernel from the raspberrypi/linux tree.

## Boot firmware

This package ships the kernel, the bcm2711 device trees and the compiled
overlays, but NOT the VideoCore boot firmware. Install `raspberrypi-firmware`
into the *target* rootfs alongside it -- a Pi will not boot without both.

It is deliberately not a dependency: the firmware belongs to the target's boot
media, and making it a dependency drags 21 MiB of Broadcom blobs into /boot on
whatever machine happens to cross-compile the kernel.

## Overlays

`make ARCH=arm64 dtbs` builds the overlays as .dtbo, reachable under
arch/arm64/boot/dts/overlays because that path is a symlink into the arm tree
where the Pi overlay sources live (arch/arm64/boot/dts/Makefile carries
`subdir-y += overlays`).

Only the compiled .dtbo files are of any use at boot -- the .dts files beside
them are source. Releases up to 6.18.33.95b85be-1 shipped the .dts by mistake,
so /boot/overlays was inert.

## Building

Needs an aarch64 cross toolchain (`aarch64-gcc`); the build script hardcodes
ARCH=arm64 CROSS_COMPILE=aarch64-linux-gnu-.
